# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env.example — OPTIONAL tuning knobs only. Copy to `.env` if you want to
# override defaults:  cp .env.example .env
#
# ⚠️  NO SECRETS GO IN THIS FILE.
#     Your API keys live in the tools that own them, NOT in the repo:
#       • DeepSeek key  → paste once in the fcc-server admin UI
#                         (http://127.0.0.1:8082/admin). It persists to
#                         ~/.fcc/.env, which ship.js also reads for graphify.
#       • OpenAI/Codex  → run `codex login` (browser OAuth or OPENAI_API_KEY).
#     `.env` is gitignored, but keep keys out of it anyway.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Token cap across all rounds before the loop escalates (default 2,000,000).
# SHIP_TOKEN_BUDGET=2000000

# Engine overrides (ADR-0004 / ADR-0009). Each role is a headless CLI command;
# swap any of them without editing ship.js. Defaults shown.
#   Carpenter (Worker) — cheap bulk builder. Default: fcc-claude (DeepSeek).
#   Set to `claude` to build with Claude instead and skip the fcc router entirely.
# SHIP_CARPENTER_CMD=fcc-claude
#   Master Carpenter (foreman) — inspects the Worker's build. Default: claude.
# SHIP_MASTER_CMD=claude
#   Reviewer — independent auditor. Default: codex.
# SHIP_REVIEWER_CMD=codex
